 "contract": "The ground: each row's args are normalised by terrainParams (shared/terrainmath.js) before the height law makeHeightField reads them, and the heights pinned are of the normalised params. A missing or non-finite number takes its default: size 80, amplitude 3, flatRadius 0, flatHeight 0, frequency 2.5; seed, default 1, is truncated toward zero and then read as a 32-bit integer (seed | 0), where 0 reads as 1; octaves is truncated and clamped to 1..8, default 4. kind: 'flat' is level ground at its height (default 0, size 200): the noise keys and shaping are then not read (no row here pins it). Any other key (scale in one row here) is not a parameter and changes nothing. Shaping (shared/terrainshape.js shapeParams) is carried only when the args use it: the first 64 features, in order; an unknown type is dropped; radius is clamped to 0..2000 and a feature with radius <= 0.05 dropped; height is clamped to -500..500; a ridge needs finite x1, z1, x2, z2, a hill or flatten finite x, z, or it is dropped; a flatten's edge defaults to radius * 0.5, clamped to 0.01..2000; a heightmap {grid, min (default 0), max (default 10)} whose grid is a stored grid's reference is carried too (no row here pins it: its grid is data outside this file). The features then apply in order over the base height (shapeHeight): the noise, or, when a heightmap's grid is found, the heightmap's sample in its place (the noise is then not read; a grid not found falls back to the noise). A row may shape its ground from beside its args, as a world does from components of their own on @world (never on level ground: kind 'flat' reads neither). named is {<name>: a feature, with order?}: read as a list feature is and applied after the list, by order (absent or non-finite: 0) and then by name in code-unit order, the first 64 of them. tiles is the sculpted layer, {<i>-<j>: {<sample>: mm}}: a lattice of samples every 0.5 m, sample (gx, gz) standing at x = -2048 + 0.5 gx, z = -2048 + 0.5 gz; tile <i>-<j> holds the 32 × 32 samples gx = 32 i …, gz = 32 j …, row-major with rows along z (sample (gx, gz) is entry (gz - 32 j) * 32 + (gx - 32 i)), in whole millimetres; a row here lists only the samples that aren't 0, and a tile or sample not given is 0. At a point the layer is bilinear between the four samples round it (u = (x - -2048) / 0.5, i = floor(u), along x first: a = d00 + (d10 - d00) * fu, b = d01 + (d11 - d01) * fu, then (a + (b - a) * fv) / 1000 metres; nothing is added where all four are 0), and it is added last, after every feature. The sky: each policy is read through normalizePolicy (shared/forecast.js) with its epoch kept, and segments are walked from the epoch, each starting where the last ended.",
 "note": "heights and intensities are IEEE-754 float64 bits, big-endian hex; times are epoch ms",
